2. Rust crate dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The resolved dependency tree comprises 260 third-party crates (excluding
  Wellfriend's own workspace crates). A `cargo metadata` license audit finds the tree
  is ENTIRELY PERMISSIVE: predominantly MIT, with some MIT, BSD,
  Zlib, Unicode-3.0, and IJG (libjpeg) components — all permissive.

  No GPL / AGPL / LGPL / MPL / EUPL / CDDL / SSPL is FORCED anywhere in the tree.
  The single crate whose license string mentions any GPL form is `r-efi`
  (MIT OR LGPL-2.1-or-later) — a tri-licensed UEFI-target crate
  from which the MIT option is taken (no copyleft forced) and which does
  not compile on the primary targets.

  COMMERCIAL-COMPATIBILITY VERDICT: the dependency tree and the bundled fonts are
  fully compatible with redistributing and SELLING this SDK under MIT OR
  Apache-2.0, including embedding in proprietary/closed-source software, with no
  copyleft obligations. (Contrast Poppler's GPLv2-family licensing.)

  NOTE: PyMuPDF (AGPL) is used ONLY as an external comparison/benchmark tool in
  the dev-time benchmark harness; it is NOT a dependency of any Wellfriend crate and
  is never linked or distributed with the SDK.

  The full per-license breakdown, the audit method, and reproduction steps are
